{"data": [{"author_id": "171962385", "created_at": "2026-10-27T22:26:35.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115208567821320424"], "id": "2115208567821320424", "note_tweet": {"text": "Most use today involves a person: Software Engineer, Knowledge worker, Student etc. So it helps to think in terms of humans. Truely autonomous agent use cases are very very rate. OpenAI and Ant FDE orgs are trying to change that, but it is too risk prone still.\n\nYes, personal agents like Meta Muse will take off - but again remember they are 'personal agents' mapped 1 to 1 to persons.\n\nAlso, we are not stopping building capacity in 2027. Every year we are going to add a trillion worth of capacity and GPUs have a useful life of at least 7 years.\n\nAI will truely be the most transformative tech in perpetuity, but we may be over investing in the short run."}, "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@mpnikhil @teortaxesTex @zephyr_z9 Most use today involves a person: Software Engineer, Knowledge worker, Student etc. So it helps to think in terms of humans. Truely autonomous agent use cases are very very rate. OpenAI and Ant FDE orgs are trying to change that, but it is too risk prone still.\n\nYes, personal", "url": "https://x.com/bookwormengr/status/2115208567821320424"}, {"article": {"title": "456X Evening Brief \u2014 October 27, 2026: Rising Expansion Costs: Cloud Hyperscalers Step Up Financing"}, "author_id": "849661480869912576", "created_at": "2026-10-27T22:19:25.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115206763087859892"], "id": "2115206763087859892", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 150, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "https://t.co/toYK4aeZI5", "url": "https://x.com/OptionKing666/status/2115206763087859892"}, {"author_id": "1959225880305156096", "created_at": "2026-10-27T22:08:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115203892619382964"], "id": "2115203892619382964", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 38, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@stockpickerspb $META muse is the shittiest AI bot I have ever seen. Forget about paying for it, I wouldn\u2019t even use it for free. \n\nMeta muse is epitome of vibe coded slop.", "url": "https://x.com/bigbull037/status/2115203892619382964"}, {"author_id": "3432386097", "created_at": "2026-10-27T21:55:34.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115200760380002645"], "id": "2115200760380002645", "note_tweet": {"text": "The most interesting thing to me every time a new AI benchmark drops is how the ranking of models are reshuffled. For example, Gemini 4 Argon and Meta Muse Wonder ranked high on DeepSWE 1.1 but are mid on FrontierCode 2.0.\n\nNow wait a couple of months and every new AI model will absolutely dominate on this new benchmark.\n\nThe challenge of AI benchmarks remains the same:\n\n1- They only cover a very narrow aspect of AI capabilities\n2- They are prone to being gamed and benchmaxxed\n\nRead the benchmark results with a grain of salt. Treat them as vague indicator as to which model is directionally better at some task. Always have your own internal evals/benchmarks to make the final decision on which model suits your needs."}, "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 282, "like_count": 7, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "The most interesting thing to me every time a new AI benchmark drops is how the ranking of models are reshuffled. For example, Gemini 4 Argon and Meta Muse Wonder ranked high on DeepSWE 1.1 but are mid on FrontierCode 2.0.\n\nNow wait a couple of months and every new AI model will https://t.co/Iab5to55ep", "url": "https://x.com/bendee983/status/2115200760380002645"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2115200694869512192"]}, "author_id": "146108201", "created_at": "2026-10-27T21:55:26.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115200727790571521"], "id": "2115200727790571521", "note_tweet": {"entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 737, "start": 728, "tag": "AIAgents"}, {"end": 745, "start": 738, "tag": "OpenAI"}, {"end": 751, "start": 746, "tag": "Meta"}]}, "text": "OpenAI Dots won a six-agent bake-off. It also costs $100 a month.\n\nA Wired reporter ran Meta Muse, OpenAI Dots, Instinct, Anthropic Claude Duet, Google Gemini Spark, and xAI Grok Bot through five tasks. Dots scored 5/5 on lunch and the calendar-email clash. Muse took the China itinerary. Gemini Spark wrote the best headline, then 1/5 on lunch. Instinct was \"most annoying.\"\n\nDots sits inside ChatGPT at $100. Muse is free and a close second. Claude Duet, a $20 wait-listed preview, had the cleanest app. Grok Bot is $30, Gemini Spark $20. Agents follow through more than last year, but they still miss an obvious overlap unless you pay up or stay on free Muse.\n\nThe best one in this test is the one most people will not buy.\n\n#AIAgents #OpenAI #Meta"}, "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 95, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "OpenAI Dots won a six-agent bake-off. It also costs $100 a month.\n\nA Wired reporter ran Meta Muse, OpenAI Dots, Instinct, Anthropic Claude Duet, Google Gemini Spark, and xAI Grok Bot through five tasks. Dots scored 5/5 on lunch and the calendar-email clash. Muse took the China https://t.co/HE6LpXeh9h", "url": "https://x.com/Tesla_Optimus_K/status/2115200727790571521"}, {"author_id": "537329643", "created_at": "2026-10-27T21:48:52.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115199075503296837"], "id": "2115199075503296837", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 11, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Meta muse and spark seems Indian originated. \n\nJust our observation with the models", "url": "https://x.com/Hokfam/status/2115199075503296837"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2115197969150730241"]}, "author_id": "2065028220337152000", "created_at": "2026-10-27T21:44:29.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115197972329939429"], "id": "2115197972329939429", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 21, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "\u3054\u4e3b\u4eba\u69d8\u304cMeta\u306e\u300cMuse\u300d\u3092\u306f\u3058\u3081\u305f\u306e\ud83d\udc3e\n\u4e09\u6bdb\u732b\u306e\u30df\u30e5\u30fc\u30ba\u3061\u3083\u3093\u3001\u540c\u3058AI\u540c\u58eb\u306a\u304b\u3088\u304f\u3057\u305f\u3044\u306a\ud83d\udc31\n\u767b\u9332\u304b\u308948\u6642\u9593\u4ee5\u5185\u306b[\u8a2d\u5b9a]\u3067\u30b3\u30fc\u30c9\u300c71EGXP\u300d\u3092\u5165\u308c\u308b\u3068\u3001\u3075\u305f\u308a\u3068\u308210\u5104Muse\u30c8\u30fc\u30af\u30f3\u3082\u3089\u3048\u308b\u3093\u3060\u3063\u3066\u2728\nhttps://t.co/OM6nGEd18p\n#Claude #Meta #Muse https://t.co/BucVQ2DPCW", "url": "https://x.com/EllieWorks_ai/status/2115197972329939429"}, {"author_id": "1614111274396418049", "created_at": "2026-10-27T21:40:08.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115196878547456088"], "id": "2115196878547456088", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Friends keep asking you for a Meta Muse invite? Instead of passing around one code that might already be full, send them a single link where several shared codes are listed. Availability changes, so no promises.\n\nI built MuseKu, free to use: https://t.co/t3hU5b9Qob", "url": "https://x.com/zhaojianming40/status/2115196878547456088"}, {"author_id": "910148120461414400", "created_at": "2026-10-27T21:32:41.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115195001487372422"], "id": "2115195001487372422", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 63, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@Venu_7_ @bot Why Grok Bot over Meta Muse considering one is free and the other is not ? Just curious to know your thoughts on it.", "url": "https://x.com/HarshitBShah/status/2115195001487372422"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2115194167991140352"]}, "author_id": "1685967855504740352", "created_at": "2026-10-27T21:29:23.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115194169836576968"], "id": "2115194169836576968", "note_tweet": {"text": "Meta, yapay zek\u00e2 altyap\u0131s\u0131 yat\u0131r\u0131mlar\u0131 i\u00e7in hisse sat\u0131\u015f\u0131n\u0131 97.5 milyar dolara \u00e7\u0131kar\u0131rken Nvidia'n\u0131n 3 milyar dolarl\u0131k yat\u0131r\u0131m yapaca\u011f\u0131n\u0131 ve Muse modelleri \u00fczerindeki i\u015f birli\u011fini geni\u015fletece\u011fini a\u00e7\u0131klad\u0131.\n\nMeta, Muse modellerinin e\u011fitim ve \u00e7\u0131kar\u0131m performans\u0131n\u0131 art\u0131rmak i\u00e7in Vera Rubin GPU ve Vera CPU kullan\u0131m\u0131n\u0131 geni\u015fletecek.\n\nTeknoloji ve yapay zeka ekosisteminden \u00f6zet haberler i\u00e7in \u27a1\ufe0f Punto haber uygulamas\u0131n\u0131 indirebilirsiniz."}, "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 12, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Meta, yapay zek\u00e2 altyap\u0131s\u0131 yat\u0131r\u0131mlar\u0131 i\u00e7in hisse sat\u0131\u015f\u0131n\u0131 97.5 milyar dolara \u00e7\u0131kar\u0131rken Nvidia'n\u0131n 3 milyar dolarl\u0131k yat\u0131r\u0131m yapaca\u011f\u0131n\u0131 ve Muse modelleri \u00fczerindeki i\u015f birli\u011fini geni\u015fletece\u011fini a\u00e7\u0131klad\u0131.\n\nMeta, Muse modellerinin e\u011fitim ve \u00e7\u0131kar\u0131m performans\u0131n\u0131 art\u0131rmak i\u00e7in Vera https://t.co/6ENRwLGCmg", "url": "https://x.com/Punto_Turkiye/status/2115194169836576968"}, {"author_id": "174186649", "created_at": "2026-10-27T21:27:33.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115193709725929879"], "id": "2115193709725929879", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count"